 * (n/a) when the person's own momentum is. quarter is scaled divided by four (rounded like every divide)
 * and tier is SINK when scaled is below zero, STEADY from 0 up to 199 and SURGE at 200 or more; both
 * null (n/a) when scaled is. keel is scaled plus twice momentum plus twice norm plus
 * thrust, null (n/a) when momentum or norm is.
 * fathom is keel plus momentum plus 68 and draft is keel plus thrust; both null (n/a) when keel is.
 * cascade is fathom plus scaled plus 72, null (n/a) when fathom is. trim is keel minus thrust, null (n/a)
 * when keel is. ripple is cascade plus keel plus 76, null (n/a) when cascade is. heading is keel plus norm,
 * null (n/a) when keel or norm is. ballast is ripple plus thrust plus 80, null (n/a) when ripple is.
 * keystone is ballast plus norm, null (n/a) when ballast or norm is. bearing is keel minus norm, null
 * (n/a) when keel or norm is. pitch is keel plus momentum, null (n/a) when keel is. tackle is keel
 * minus momentum, null (n/a) when keel is. yaw is keel plus scaled, null (n/a) when keel is. heave
 * is keel minus scaled, null (n/a) when keel is. camber is keel plus 200, null (n/a) when keel is.
 * sheer is keel minus 100, null (n/a) when keel is. beam is keel times three, null (n/a) when keel is.
 * freeboard is keel divided by three (rounded like every divide), null (n/a) when keel is. buoyancy is
 * keel times three, null (n/a) when keel is. knot is keel divided by three (rounded like every
